# Forge recipes (code host)

Path after install: `~/.agents/skills/system_assets/forge.md` (catalog skill: `system_assets`).
Skills under `~/.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md` point here for host-specific commands.

{% if features.github | default('false') == 'true' %}
## Host: GitHub (`gh`)

Requires `gh` CLI + repo access. Prefer `gh` over raw curl for API work.

### Discover context
```bash
git remote -v
git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD
git rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name @{u}
```

### Fetch PR / MR context
```bash
gh pr view URL --json number,title,headRefName,baseRefName,commits,files,reviews,url
gh pr diff PR_NUMBER
gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/PR_NUMBER --jq '.title'
```

### Fetch review / issue comments
```bash
# review comment (#discussion_rID)
gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/comments/ID
# issue/PR timeline (#issuecomment-ID)
gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/issues/comments/ID
# all PR review comments
gh api repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/PR_NUMBER/comments --paginate \
  --jq '[.[] | {id, body, path, line, original_line, diff_hunk, user: .user.login, created_at, in_reply_to_id, pull_request_review_id, html_url}]'
```

### Unresolved review threads
```bash
gh api graphql -f query='
{
  repository(owner: "OWNER", name: "REPO") {
    pullRequest(number: PR_NUMBER) {
      reviewThreads(first: 100) {
        nodes {
          id
          isResolved
          isOutdated
          comments(first: 1) {
            nodes { databaseId }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}'
```

Keep only root comments (`in_reply_to_id` null) whose thread is not resolved and not outdated, with a valid line.

### Post / edit PR body / comments
```bash
# top-level PR comment
gh pr comment PR_NUMBER --body "..."
# edit PR description (additive only — callers rebuild full body)
gh pr view PR --json body -q .body
gh pr edit PR --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
...full body...
EOF
)"
# approve
gh pr review PR_NUMBER --approve --body "..."
```

For nested review-thread replies and resolve/minimize, use GraphQL after user confirms (see `/comment-reply` workflow). Capture `html_url` from create responses.

### Resolve thread
```bash
gh api graphql -f query='mutation { resolveReviewThread(input: {threadId: "THREAD_NODE_ID"}) { thread { isResolved } } }'
```

### Commit / PR links
```text
https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/commit/SHA
https://github.com/OWNER/REPO/pull/N
```

### CI — list / trigger / watch
```bash
branch="$(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref --symbolic-full-name @{u} | sed 's#^[^/]*/##')"
gh workflow list
gh workflow run WORKFLOW --ref "$branch"
gh workflow view WORKFLOW --yaml
gh workflow run WORKFLOW --ref "$branch" -f key=value
gh run list --branch "$branch" --workflow WORKFLOW --limit 5
gh run list --branch "$branch" --limit 10
gh run view RUN_ID --log-failed
gh run view --web
gh run watch RUN_ID
# optional local aliases
ciopen
ciwatch
```

### Activity search (progress report)
```bash
gh search commits --author @me --committer-date ">=YYYY-MM-DD"
gh search prs --author @me --updated ">=YYYY-MM-DD"
gh search issues --commenter @me --updated ">=YYYY-MM-DD"
```

